{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#613","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#613","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#613\",\"parent_revision\":\"50132c2dcd8b27614aa0be15051f9b1ca31c27949cb7345cb4943a563a13eace\",\"root_revision\":\"50132c2dcd8b27614aa0be15051f9b1ca31c27949cb7345cb4943a563a13eace\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Refactor\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: 2026-05-16\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe `_get_table_width(table: Table) -> int` function is identically defined in 6 scripts:\\\\n- .claude/skills/session-historian/scripts/session_query.py\\\\n- .claude/skills/backlog/scripts/backlog.py\\\\n- .claude/utilities/find-temp-documentation.py\\\\n- plugins/plugin-creator/scripts/normalize_frontmatter.py\\\\n- plugins/plugin-creator/scripts/create_plugin.py\\\\n- plugins/python3-development/scripts/validate_pep723.py\\\\n\\\\nExtract to a shared utility module and import from all 6.\\\\n\\\\nDiscovered during code review session 2026-03-11.\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAssessment date: 2026-04-23\\n\\n| # | Condition | Status | Source |\\n|---|-----------|--------|--------|\\n| 1 | 6 source files confirmed | AVAILABLE | Issue description (2026-03-11 code review) |\\n| 2 | Shared utility location | DERIVABLE | `.claude/utilities/` is the existing home for cross-plugin Python utilities (e.g., `find-temp-documentation.py`) |\\n| 3 | Import mechanism for PEP 723 standalone scripts | DERIVABLE | Use `sys.path.insert(0, ...)` + `importlib` or restructure as package import; established pattern in repo |\\n| 4 | Function is pure (no side effects, safe to extract) | AVAILABLE | `_get_table_width(table: Table) -> int` \u2014 read-only computation |\\n| 5 | No test coverage to update | AVAILABLE | All 6 scripts are CLI tools; no unit tests reference this function directly |\\n\\nVerdict: READY \u2014 all conditions AVAILABLE or DERIVABLE. Pure mechanical refactor, low risk.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **maintainer of the codebase**, I want to **extract shared _get_table_width() utility from 6 duplicate copies** so that **the code is cleaner and more maintainable**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Code review 2026-03-11\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-11\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-23)\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\nP2 Refactor. 6 scripts modified + 1 new file created. Zero behavioral change \u2014 pure extraction. Low risk. Reduces maintenance burden: future changes to `_get_table_width` need to be made in one place instead of six.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- Create shared utility module (e.g., `.claude/utilities/rich_utils.py` or `plugins/shared/scripts/rich_utils.py`) containing `_get_table_width(table: Table) -> int`\\n- All 6 scripts import from the shared module instead of defining their own copy\\n- Function signature `_get_table_width(table: Table) -> int` is unchanged \u2014 no behavioral difference\\n- All 6 scripts continue to execute correctly after the refactor\\n- No other copies of this function remain in the codebase\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n- `.claude/skills/session-historian/scripts/session_query.py` \u2014 defines `_get_table_width`, import to replace\\n- `.claude/skills/backlog/scripts/backlog.py` \u2014 defines `_get_table_width`, import to replace\\n- `.claude/utilities/find-temp-documentation.py` \u2014 defines `_get_table_width`, import to replace\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/scripts/normalize_frontmatter.py` \u2014 defines `_get_table_width`, import to replace\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/scripts/create_plugin.py` \u2014 defines `_get_table_width`, import to replace\\n- `plugins/python3-development/scripts/validate_pep723.py` \u2014 defines `_get_table_width`, import to replace\\n- `.claude/utilities/rich_utils.py` \u2014 new shared utility (to create)\\n\\n### Grooming Notes\\n\\nPlan P46dd3c2a is blocked \u2014 re-scope required before implementation.\\n\\nThe three plugin scripts (plugins/plugin-creator/scripts/normalize_frontmatter.py, create_plugin.py, plugins/python3-development/scripts/validate_pep723.py) run inside the plugin cache after installation with no access to .claude/utilities/. The sys.path.insert approach in the plan only works in the development repo \u2014 it breaks after distribution.\\n\\nThe .claude/ scripts (session-historian, utilities/) can share a utility at .claude/utilities/rich_utils.py. The plugin scripts cannot participate. Re-scope options: duplicate the function inside each plugin bundle, or accept the duplication for plugin scripts and only deduplicate the .claude/ scripts.\\n\\nSee plugins/development-harness/docs/plugin-deployment-model.md for the zip-and-move constraint.\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs a developer maintaining scripts, I need `_get_table_width()` extracted to a single shared utility so that I don't maintain 6 identical copies of the same function across 6 separate scripts.\\n\",\"digest\":\"8c7a8f0fce7bdb20861fe31bb7e60a42d1cefeedc8eaa2784335441d654af2ae\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCOUKA\"}"}